      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the current SMMUv3 upstream driver, I see that\u0027s it\u0027s possible to make EL1 handle everything and just let EL2 send resume/abort.\n\nI am wondering, if we can just rely on `kvm_iommu_nested_cfg_sync` \nfor that. It already have a very similar declaration, and it\u0027s up to the driver how to decoded the passed descriptor. what do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d29fdf5c506e9b2897fe08478af3805aef790285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3287686c_965a3c06",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
