        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T17:40:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, that\u0027s how it\u0027d be implemented. With regards to `kvm_iommu_nested_cfg_sync()`, how would the EL2 IOMMU driver distinguish between a nested_cfg_sync descriptior, and a page response descriptor? You could use the size, but that seems fragile. We could extend and probably rename `nested_cfg_sync` so that it takes in a command as well so that it can interpret the structure and validate it, like an `ioctl()` handler?",
      "parentUuid": "481cc45a_95735881",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d29fdf5c506e9b2897fe08478af3805aef790285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
